WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:39.092
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:39.362 --> 01:41.362
[Episode 39]

3
02:11.386 --> 02:13.073
Have an apple.

4
02:17.520 --> 02:18.960
Not talking to me?

5
02:22.206 --> 02:24.399
You don't have to pretend with me.

6
02:25.640 --> 02:27.580
I know you're awake.

7
02:35.946 --> 02:41.427
Is there really nothing that can still get through to you?

8
02:49.400 --> 02:51.493
I nearly forgot it.

9
02:52.200 --> 02:57.680
The day your child died, I was at the hospital.

10
02:57.680 --> 02:59.659
I could have saved him.

11
03:11.720 --> 03:12.926
What?

12
03:14.320 --> 03:15.679
What did you say?

13
03:18.027 --> 03:20.427
Why would I ever let him live,

14
03:20.427 --> 03:24.687
when he had been a reminder that he was your child with Yu Chang Xuan?

15
03:28.026 --> 03:31.086
Only with that cursed child gone

16
03:31.086 --> 03:37.086
would there be nothing left between us.

17
03:37.907 --> 03:40.526
Only with him dead

18
03:40.526 --> 03:47.240
could you belong to me completely.

19
03:47.240 --> 03:49.941
Jiang Xue Ting, I'll kill you!

20
04:09.840 --> 04:11.720
Why?

21
04:11.720 --> 04:13.153
Ping Jun...

22
04:15.266 --> 04:17.769
I'd be glad to die...

23
04:17.769 --> 04:22.060
if you're the one who kills me.

24
04:35.986 --> 04:37.686
Don't cry.

25
04:42.267 --> 04:47.186
Your child is still alive.

26
04:48.787 --> 04:50.327
What did you say?

27
04:51.767 --> 04:53.386
Zi Yi said...

28
04:54.400 --> 04:56.420
Xie Zao Hua...

29
04:58.727 --> 05:03.167
secretly took your child out of the hospital

30
05:04.480 --> 05:06.399
and brought him to Nanhuai.

31
05:15.027 --> 05:18.760
Then why did you lie and tell me my child was dead?

32
05:35.746 --> 05:38.806
I blew up Fujiwara's factory.

33
05:38.806 --> 05:41.027
Many Japanese died.

34
05:41.027 --> 05:43.446
They won't rest until I'm dead.

35
05:44.320 --> 05:50.000
I've done too many wrong things in my life.

36
05:51.467 --> 05:54.366
And you're the one I've hurt the most.

37
05:55.680 --> 05:57.099
In the end,

38
05:58.520 --> 06:03.053
I want to die at your hands.

39
06:15.320 --> 06:17.419
Here's the pass.

40
06:19.227 --> 06:20.793
Take it.

41
06:23.680 --> 06:25.440
Get out of the city.

42
06:26.546 --> 06:27.946
Go find him.

43
06:31.587 --> 06:33.306
Hurry!

44
06:33.306 --> 06:35.347
You're running out of time.

45
06:39.926 --> 06:41.467
Go.

46
06:42.566 --> 06:44.227
Go now!

47
06:54.486 --> 06:55.886
Ping Jun...

48
06:57.407 --> 07:03.980
You're finally free.

49
07:11.986 --> 07:15.407
Xue Ting, I read your letter today.

50
07:15.407 --> 07:17.000
It struck me like a clap of thunder.

51
07:17.000 --> 07:20.910
You are abroad, pursuing knowledge to make China rise,

52
07:20.910 --> 07:24.347
and I dare not waste my days at the girls' school either.

53
07:24.347 --> 07:26.006
Today our teacher said,

54
07:26.006 --> 07:28.587
"When the young are strong, the nation is strong,"

55
07:28.587 --> 07:30.806
and I thought of you.

56
07:30.806 --> 07:35.727
I believe you will become one of the pillars of this nation in these troubled times.

57
07:35.727 --> 07:38.306
The winter plum blossom is said to represent steadfastness

58
07:38.306 --> 07:40.827
so I embroidered a handkerchief with it,

59
07:40.827 --> 07:44.599
only hoping you'll return soon and realize your grand ambitions.

60
07:45.486 --> 07:48.446
Xue Ting, all is well at home.

61
07:48.446 --> 07:52.366
Mother made your favorite osmanthus cakes yesterday

62
07:52.366 --> 07:54.886
and said she was waiting for you to come home and taste them.

63
07:54.886 --> 07:56.480
I also have some good news.

64
07:56.480 --> 08:01.306
The modern drama I wrote, Nora's Rebirth, was staged at the girls' school.

65
08:01.306 --> 08:03.847
Our teacher praised it for its strength and conviction,

66
08:03.847 --> 08:05.760
and I want more people to know

67
08:05.760 --> 08:10.440
that whether man or woman, a person can take charge of their own fate.

68
08:11.886 --> 08:13.407
Awaiting your return.

69
09:20.160 --> 09:23.620
Master Chang Xuan, the Jiang's Residence is just ahead.

70
09:35.547 --> 09:36.766
Next.

71
09:55.120 --> 09:58.480
Chang Xuan, we've searched every corner of Jiang City.

72
09:58.480 --> 10:00.513
Still no sign of Lady Ping Jun.

73
10:12.382 --> 10:14.382
[For Chang Xuan, from Jun Dai Ti]

74
10:26.107 --> 10:30.227
By the time you read this, I'll have left Nanhuai.

75
10:31.040 --> 10:34.870
During these days by your side, I won't pretend I never thought

76
10:34.870 --> 10:39.637
that one day I might replace Ye Ping Jun in your heart.

77
10:39.637 --> 10:45.657
But the longer I stayed, the clearer I saw that your heart has always belonged to her,

78
10:45.657 --> 10:47.633
and no one else can squeeze in.

79
10:48.846 --> 10:51.080
I'm not leaving because it hurts.

80
10:51.080 --> 10:54.840
I'm leaving because it suddenly struck me that in this war-torn world,

81
10:54.840 --> 10:58.958
with so many people suffering and so many left with no home,

82
10:58.958 --> 11:05.167
if I kept going in circles over a hopeless love, I'd be thinking too small.

83
11:05.167 --> 11:09.777
I've always believed a person has to live for something.

84
11:09.777 --> 11:12.190
I used to think you were that something.

85
11:12.190 --> 11:16.840
Now I want to see if I can help more people.

86
11:16.840 --> 11:20.560
The more turbulent the times, the more we're needed.

87
11:20.560 --> 11:22.640
What I can do may not be much,

88
11:22.640 --> 11:24.699
but it's better than being stuck inside these walls.

89
11:25.520 --> 11:28.733
I believe you'll support me.

90
11:29.560 --> 11:32.741
Wherever we end up, take care of yourself.

91
12:09.206 --> 12:11.127
Newspapers! Get your newspapers!

92
12:11.127 --> 12:13.240
Newspapers!

93
12:13.240 --> 12:15.120
Japan's pouring troops into Manchuria!

94
12:15.120 --> 12:18.300
Fighting could break out there any minute!

95
12:31.960 --> 12:33.619
You want this?

96
12:39.120 --> 12:42.520
Here, the big one is for you.

97
12:42.520 --> 12:43.721
Go on.

98
12:49.000 --> 12:51.280
Thank you, miss.

99
12:53.560 --> 12:56.200
I have a child too.

100
13:03.040 --> 13:07.246
Once we get over this ridge, Nanjing won't be far.

101
13:07.246 --> 13:09.087
That's right.

102
13:09.087 --> 13:13.526
We've been fleeing south to stay alive.

103
13:14.252 --> 13:19.040
Miss, I see you've been on your own this whole trip.

104
13:19.040 --> 13:22.846
Are you going to Nanjing to find your relatives, or to Shanghai?

105
13:23.807 --> 13:25.560
I'm going to Nanhuai.

106
13:25.560 --> 13:28.341
What? Nanhuai?

107
13:29.240 --> 13:32.047
Girl, have you lost your mind?

108
13:32.047 --> 13:34.107
Everyone's running south as fast as they can.

109
13:34.107 --> 13:38.207
Nanhuai is a key town in Sujing, practically right under the Japanese nose.

110
13:38.207 --> 13:40.067
And you're heading back against the crowd?

111
13:40.067 --> 13:45.067
Yes, miss, heading north and you'll get yourself killed.

112
13:45.067 --> 13:48.626
Exactly. Why are you going north?

113
13:48.626 --> 13:54.607
My husband and my child are there.

114
13:59.920 --> 14:03.480
If I can't get back to them,

115
14:05.067 --> 14:10.227
then no matter where I go, I'll never really be home.

116
14:58.207 --> 14:59.607
Don't cry.

117
14:59.607 --> 15:01.026
Don't cry.

118
15:07.447 --> 15:08.866
Don't cry.

119
15:14.006 --> 15:15.646
Don't cry.

120
15:22.280 --> 15:23.946
- Kill! - Kill!

121
15:23.946 --> 15:25.846
- One, two, one! - Kill!

122
15:25.846 --> 15:28.067
- Defend our country! - Defend our country!

123
15:28.067 --> 15:29.920
- Move! All of you, move! - Kill!

124
15:29.920 --> 15:31.480
- One, two, one! - Keep up!

125
15:31.480 --> 15:32.767
- Kill! - Kill!

126
15:32.767 --> 15:35.147
- Run! - Defend our country!

127
15:35.147 --> 15:36.246
- Kill! - Kill!

128
15:36.246 --> 15:39.120
Chang Xuan, an urgent telegram from beyond Shanhaiguan.

129
15:39.120 --> 15:40.570
Over the past month,

130
15:40.570 --> 15:44.360
the Japanese have been stepping up drills along the South Manchuria Railway.

131
15:44.360 --> 15:45.880
Before, it was only during the day.

132
15:45.880 --> 15:47.640
Now they're at it at night too.

133
15:47.640 --> 15:50.760
They've even crossed into our security zone without warning more than once,

134
15:50.760 --> 15:55.044
A wolf sharpens its teeth before it goes for the kill.

135
15:55.044 --> 15:56.329
Pass the order.

136
15:56.329 --> 15:59.722
All defense zones are to go to Level One Alert.

137
15:59.722 --> 16:01.213
- Kill! - Yes, sir!

138
16:02.440 --> 16:03.580
- Kill! - Kill!

139
16:05.960 --> 16:07.437
The men we sent out...

140
16:07.437 --> 16:10.600
Our men have searched around Jiang City and at every checkpoint.

141
16:10.600 --> 16:12.259
Still no sign of Lady Ping Jun.

142
16:17.880 --> 16:21.760
We've been searching for so long with no word.

143
16:21.760 --> 16:23.440
I mean, if...

144
16:23.440 --> 16:25.593
- Could she have-- - No.

145
16:27.200 --> 16:28.660
I have a feeling.

146
16:30.986 --> 16:32.586
Ping Jun isn't dead.

147
16:33.846 --> 16:35.866
She's alive.

148
16:35.866 --> 16:38.067
I think so too.

149
16:38.067 --> 16:40.267
- But what if-- - There's no what if.

150
16:40.267 --> 16:43.486
If I can't find her in a day, I'll search for a day.

151
16:43.486 --> 16:47.466
A year, I'll search for a year.

152
16:47.466 --> 16:52.206
Five years, 10 years, 20 years.

153
16:53.466 --> 16:59.307
As long as I still draw breath, I'll keep searching.

154
17:00.187 --> 17:01.387
- Kill! - Kill!

155
17:13.000 --> 17:15.013
Ze Ning, come play with us.

156
17:24.280 --> 17:29.017
Mother, Qi Xuan says she got to the field hospital on the outskirts of Beixin safely

157
17:29.017 --> 17:30.680
and is working there as a nurse.

158
17:30.680 --> 17:34.000
She says everything's settled and we're not to worry.

159
17:34.880 --> 17:36.470
She's something else.

160
17:36.470 --> 17:42.130
Leaves a letter and runs off to find Xiao Bei Chen.

161
17:42.130 --> 17:45.360
Nothing can stop her.

162
17:45.360 --> 17:48.600
Mother, you know what Qi Xuan's like.

163
17:48.600 --> 17:52.560
Walls in her room are covered with newspaper clippings about Xiao Bei Chen,

164
17:52.560 --> 17:55.080
and her drawers are stuffed with them too.

165
17:55.080 --> 17:58.360
That name's been carved into her heart for years.

166
17:59.287 --> 18:03.686
A field hospital in the rear is relatively safe.

167
18:04.960 --> 18:10.287
She's doing what she wants. Of course she's happy.

168
18:10.287 --> 18:12.807
As long as it's her wish,

169
18:12.807 --> 18:18.007
I'd support her even if she chased the moon to the ends of the earth.

170
18:18.007 --> 18:21.126
I'll stay home and wait.

171
18:21.126 --> 18:26.426
As long as she's safe, she can come back whenever she likes.

172
18:28.886 --> 18:30.507
Brother is back.

173
18:32.487 --> 18:34.346
Daddy, pick me up.

174
18:34.346 --> 18:35.926
Xiao Yu Er.

175
18:35.926 --> 18:39.007
- You're back so late today. - Indeed.

176
18:39.007 --> 18:40.120
Get some rest.

177
18:40.120 --> 18:43.019
Uncle, did you bring me a treat?

178
18:43.760 --> 18:47.214
- Thank you, Uncle. - Don't mention it. Share it with the others.

179
18:48.186 --> 18:50.507
- Has Xiao Yu Er been good today? - Yes.

180
18:50.507 --> 18:53.920
I listen to Grandma and Auntie.

181
18:53.920 --> 18:55.200
Really?

182
18:57.160 --> 19:00.129
He's been waiting for you all day.

183
19:00.129 --> 19:02.026
Kept saying he wanted Daddy's hug.

184
19:12.680 --> 19:15.164
Daddy, I want a story.

185
19:15.164 --> 19:17.424
I'll continue the story of Peter Pan.

186
19:20.760 --> 19:25.097
Wendy and her brothers flew with Peter Pan,

187
19:25.097 --> 19:30.000
on and on, far, far away.

188
19:30.000 --> 19:33.740
Finally, they flew back home,

189
19:35.040 --> 19:39.519
and they saw that the window was still open.

190
19:40.400 --> 19:45.280
Peter Pan told them that as long as the children were still out there,

191
19:45.280 --> 19:50.320
their mother would never shut that window,

192
19:50.320 --> 19:56.161
because she was afraid they wouldn't be able to get in when they came home.

193
19:57.846 --> 20:00.707
Daddy, I miss Mommy too.

194
20:15.626 --> 20:18.247
Xiao Yu Er's eyes are so bright.

195
20:19.267 --> 20:21.546
They look just like Mommy's.

196
20:22.360 --> 20:29.039
And this little nose and little mouth are just like hers.

197
20:29.760 --> 20:33.840
Mommy will be so happy to see you.

198
20:33.840 --> 20:38.513
Then let's leave the window open for Mommy too, shall we?

199
20:41.760 --> 20:43.060
Sure.

200
20:50.120 --> 20:51.721
I promise you,

201
20:54.346 --> 20:59.707
I'll make sure Xiao Yu Er sees Mommy as soon as he can.

202
21:09.680 --> 21:13.007
On the night of September 18, 1931,

203
21:13.007 --> 21:18.200
Japanese artillery opened fire by Liutiao Lake and shelled the Northern Grand Barracks.

204
21:18.200 --> 21:24.240
The government sat by as the country was lost and ordered the army not to resist.

205
21:24.240 --> 21:29.240
30 million Chinese became slaves in their own land overnight.

206
21:29.240 --> 21:31.046
Move! Out of the way!

207
21:31.046 --> 21:36.640
The once-thriving city of Nanhuai lay under the shadow of impending disaster,

208
21:36.640 --> 21:40.707
with prices soaring and fear in every heart.

209
21:40.707 --> 21:42.306
What's going on?

210
21:42.306 --> 21:43.826
What happened?

211
21:58.560 --> 22:00.240
Deputy Commander.

212
22:00.240 --> 22:01.684
The firing slits are too high.

213
22:01.684 --> 22:03.173
Lower the angle.

214
22:03.840 --> 22:06.489
Those barricades aren't anchored deep enough. They won't hold up to a charge.

215
22:06.489 --> 22:08.143
Reinforce them.

216
22:08.143 --> 22:10.276
Yes, sir. We'll fix it at once.

217
22:10.276 --> 22:11.613
Drive them deeper.

218
22:13.840 --> 22:15.643
Line up! Line up!

219
22:15.643 --> 22:16.886
One at a time.

220
22:16.886 --> 22:18.060
Thank you.

221
22:19.160 --> 22:21.487
Here, take it. Hold on to it.

222
22:21.487 --> 22:24.600
- Thank you. - Don't push. Plenty for all.

223
22:24.600 --> 22:26.270
- Next. - Thank you.

224
22:26.270 --> 22:27.270
Next.

225
22:28.280 --> 22:29.280
Line up!

226
22:46.167 --> 22:47.467
Stop the car.

227
23:21.360 --> 23:26.646
[Xiangxi Hotel]

228
24:57.000 --> 24:58.736
Japanese planes!

229
24:58.736 --> 25:00.806
- Up there! - Run!

230
25:00.806 --> 25:03.487
- Take cover! - This way!

231
25:03.487 --> 25:05.207
Drop that! Get up!

232
25:05.207 --> 25:06.946
Hurry, take cover!

233
25:14.527 --> 25:16.606
Take cover!

234
25:27.207 --> 25:28.646
Run!

235
25:30.520 --> 25:36.633
Every bank, post office, and school basement has an air-raid shelter. Go!

236
25:42.546 --> 25:44.086
Run this way! Hurry!

237
25:44.086 --> 25:46.126
Help everyone. Get them to the shelters!

238
25:46.126 --> 25:47.786
- Yes, sir. - Take cover!

239
25:47.786 --> 25:49.846
- Keep up! - This way! Hurry!

240
25:49.846 --> 25:52.066
Don't panic! This way!

241
25:52.066 --> 25:53.586
Don't stop! Move!

242
25:53.586 --> 25:54.606
Get into the shelter!

243
25:54.606 --> 25:56.360
Hurry, take cover!

244
25:56.360 --> 25:59.267
- Keep running! Move! - Take cover!

245
25:59.267 --> 26:00.886
Everyone, take cover!

246
26:19.000 --> 26:21.153
- Get her to the shelter! - Yes, sir!

247
27:11.960 --> 27:13.060
This way.

248
27:17.366 --> 27:18.727
Ping Jun.

249
27:24.280 --> 27:25.679
Chang Xuan.

250
27:40.160 --> 27:41.786
Ping Jun!

251
29:50.146 --> 29:51.586
Are you hurt?

252
29:57.667 --> 29:59.187
I'm fine.

253
30:04.286 --> 30:05.806
I'm all right.

254
30:26.613 --> 30:28.033
You're back.

255
30:29.440 --> 30:30.759
You're back.

256
30:37.007 --> 30:38.527
Yes, I'm back.

257
30:46.440 --> 30:48.319
I'm back.

258
30:52.040 --> 30:53.786
What matters is that you're back.

259
31:06.960 --> 31:09.640
This time, the Japanese raided Nanhuai with a bomber formation.

260
31:09.640 --> 31:11.686
They dropped their bombs and pulled out fast.

261
31:11.686 --> 31:13.487
No ground troops have moved in yet.

262
31:13.487 --> 31:15.286
Since September 18,

263
31:16.267 --> 31:19.280
the Japanese have rolled through the Northeast unopposed.

264
31:19.280 --> 31:25.240
But inside Shanhaiguan, they're not ready to get bogged down in an all-out war just yet.

265
31:25.240 --> 31:29.507
This bombing was to intimidate us.

266
31:29.507 --> 31:35.107
They want to tell Nanhuai that resistance means death.

267
31:35.800 --> 31:39.080
They even want to force us to retreat without a fight,

268
31:39.080 --> 31:40.320
just like the Northeast Army did.

269
31:40.320 --> 31:42.440
- The Japanese are despicable! - They're going too far!

270
31:42.440 --> 31:43.527
Indeed.

271
31:43.527 --> 31:45.747
- So despicable! - Right, they've gone too far.

272
31:45.747 --> 31:47.727
- This is intolerable. - That's outrageous!

273
31:47.727 --> 31:51.106
Chang Xuan, what do you think?

274
31:52.000 --> 31:55.601
Not long ago, I pulled a little boy out of the rubble.

275
31:57.086 --> 31:59.053
He wasn't even as tall as our rifles,

276
32:00.280 --> 32:03.866
and he asked me if he was going to die.

277
32:04.920 --> 32:07.000
Now, there are still people who believe

278
32:07.000 --> 32:10.520
that as long as we don't provoke the Japanese, and don't strike first,

279
32:10.520 --> 32:12.737
Nanhuai can stay safe in its corner.

280
32:12.737 --> 32:15.097
They are still clinging to that fantasy.

281
32:16.120 --> 32:22.077
Whether or not the Japanese attack Nanhuai, every inch of ground they take is China's land.

282
32:22.077 --> 32:23.838
In a situation like this,

283
32:24.680 --> 32:29.513
holding on to even a shred of hope that we can avoid it is nothing but digging our own grave.

284
32:34.760 --> 32:37.059
Japan has invaded the three provinces of Northeast China,

285
32:37.686 --> 32:39.480
and now they've bombed Nanhuai.

286
32:39.480 --> 32:42.500
Their intent is vicious and their ambition is ruthless.

287
32:43.360 --> 32:44.906
There's no mistaking it.

288
32:45.480 --> 32:49.797
There is already a hatred between us that can never be reconciled.

289
32:49.797 --> 32:54.920
In times like these, we have to stay battle-ready.

290
32:54.920 --> 32:58.750
If the Japanese dare come, we hit them back hard.

291
32:58.750 --> 33:00.600
Defending this land is our duty.

292
33:00.600 --> 33:01.880
We will not take a single step back.

293
33:01.880 --> 33:03.005
- Right! - Not a single step back.

294
33:03.005 --> 33:04.880
- Fight back! - Fight back!

295
33:04.880 --> 33:07.660
- Yes, fight back! - Fight back!

296
34:05.346 --> 34:07.187
Master Chong Ye, slow down.

297
34:08.320 --> 34:09.953
Master Chong Ye, slow down.

298
34:49.387 --> 34:51.027
Xiao Yu Er.

299
35:24.920 --> 35:26.986
Mommy, don't cry.

300
35:38.600 --> 35:40.461
Do you recognize me?

301
35:41.586 --> 35:43.126
You're my mommy.

302
35:43.126 --> 35:46.447
You look just like the mommy in my dreams.

303
35:57.726 --> 35:59.146
Xiao Yu Er.

304
36:03.387 --> 36:05.427
Mommy's back.

305
36:07.000 --> 36:09.579
Mommy, don't cry.

306
36:24.907 --> 36:26.126
This way.

307
36:28.640 --> 36:30.007
Here, Ping Jun.

308
36:30.007 --> 36:31.266
Eat up.

309
36:36.120 --> 36:41.960
Ping Jun, you've had it rough these past years.

310
36:41.960 --> 36:47.066
Mother, now that I'm back with Chang Xuan and Xiao Yu Er,

311
36:47.066 --> 36:50.400
none of it matters.

312
36:52.266 --> 36:53.546
Eat up.

313
37:01.106 --> 37:02.387
Keep up!

314
37:02.387 --> 37:03.427
Coming.

315
37:06.880 --> 37:07.880
Here.

316
37:45.000 --> 37:46.060
Father.

317
37:49.787 --> 37:52.613
Looks like I won't be crossing this bridge tonight.

318
37:55.266 --> 37:57.467
You don't have to keep avoiding her.

319
37:57.467 --> 38:00.927
I've told Ping Jun everything.

320
38:01.720 --> 38:03.313
I didn't want to hide it from her.

321
38:10.080 --> 38:15.840
I'm prepared for her not to consider me family anymore.

322
38:15.840 --> 38:17.639
She does intend that.

323
38:18.880 --> 38:23.433
She said she doesn't owe forgiveness to someone who tried to kill her.

324
38:24.640 --> 38:29.399
She came back to the Yu's Mansion so the three of us could be together.

325
38:32.160 --> 38:34.520
From now on, if you run into each other in the house,

326
38:34.520 --> 38:36.580
you'll just have to keep things civil.

327
38:39.120 --> 38:40.241
I see.

328
38:41.440 --> 38:46.220
It hasn't been easy for the three of you to be together again.

329
38:48.560 --> 38:49.960
Don't worry.

330
38:51.160 --> 38:53.100
I know what to do.

331
38:59.720 --> 39:05.840
Wendy and her brothers flew to the windowsill of their home and looked inside.

332
39:05.840 --> 39:10.527
There was Mrs. Darling, sitting in that familiar room.

333
39:10.527 --> 39:15.166
Wendy pushed open the window that had never been shut

334
39:15.166 --> 39:19.953
and called out, "Mother, we're back!"

335
39:21.040 --> 39:27.246
Mrs. Darling woke up and held her children tight.

336
39:27.246 --> 39:30.480
Daddy, you told me this story last time.

337
39:30.480 --> 39:32.717
That's right. You remembered?

338
39:32.717 --> 39:35.680
I remembered. Back then Mommy wasn't home yet,

339
39:35.680 --> 39:38.686
and you said that as long as the window stayed open,

340
39:38.686 --> 39:41.720
Mommy would definitely come back.

341
39:41.720 --> 39:46.213
You also said you'd make sure I got to see her.

342
39:48.000 --> 39:49.560
I'm so happy now.

343
39:49.560 --> 39:51.450
Mommy did come back.

344
39:51.450 --> 39:54.553
Now I have a daddy and a mommy.

345
40:16.246 --> 40:17.566
Ping Jun.

346
40:20.186 --> 40:24.447
I'm sorry it took me so long to find you.

347
40:28.320 --> 40:31.520
Every time the withdrawal hit,

348
40:32.960 --> 40:37.400
the pain cut right down into my bones.

349
40:39.000 --> 40:41.161
Every time, I thought,

350
40:42.840 --> 40:44.619
I'm too tired,

351
40:46.307 --> 40:48.027
just let it go,

352
40:49.686 --> 40:52.027
just close my eyes and be done with it.

353
40:55.766 --> 40:57.746
But every time,

354
40:59.407 --> 41:02.827
it felt like I could hear you calling my name.

355
41:03.960 --> 41:05.940
I could hear

356
41:09.680 --> 41:12.599
Xiao Yu Er calling for his mommy.

357
41:15.246 --> 41:20.527
You two kept pulling me back out of the abyss,

358
41:21.847 --> 41:24.807
again and again.

359
41:34.246 --> 41:36.766
You went through so much for us,

360
41:39.440 --> 41:41.760
day after day, and you kept holding on.

361
41:48.347 --> 41:50.226
It wasn't holding on.

362
41:51.967 --> 41:53.927
It was the two of you.

363
41:55.427 --> 41:57.746
I couldn't bear to let go of you.

364
41:58.760 --> 42:01.620
Knowing you were waiting for me

365
42:04.787 --> 42:07.387
was what kept me going.

366
42:23.226 --> 42:26.847
In a year and more since the September 18 Incident,

367
42:26.847 --> 42:29.246
the entire Northeast had fallen.

368
42:29.246 --> 42:32.307
The Japanese had installed the puppet state of Manchukuo,

369
42:32.307 --> 42:34.646
and their ambitions hardly stopped there.

370
42:34.646 --> 42:36.467
In January 1933,

371
42:36.467 --> 42:38.447
Japanese forces attacked Shanhaiguan.

372
42:38.447 --> 42:40.640
By early March, Chengde had fallen,

373
42:40.640 --> 42:44.360
and all of Rehe was lost.

374
42:44.360 --> 42:45.764
According to the battle reports,

375
42:45.764 --> 42:48.547
the Japanese main force is pushing toward the Great Wall's passes.

376
42:48.547 --> 42:49.827
The Central Army and the Northwest Army

377
42:49.827 --> 42:52.927
have been locked in back-and-forth fighting with the Japanese at Wubeikou.

378
42:53.787 --> 42:57.787
The casualties are devastating, but they haven't yielded an inch.

379
42:57.787 --> 43:00.106
The defenders at Wubeikou are running out of ammunition,

380
43:00.106 --> 43:02.867
with over 10,000 dead and wounded, and they need reinforcements now.

381
43:02.867 --> 43:06.577
If we could send troops north and dig in at the Great Wall passes,

382
43:06.577 --> 43:09.057
we might still be able to hold the Japanese outside the Wall.

383
43:16.040 --> 43:17.660
This is Wubeikou.

384
43:18.867 --> 43:24.166
No matter how brutal the battle gets there, that's the Central Army's business.

385
43:24.166 --> 43:30.200
The Yu Army is not throwing itself into that bottomless pit.

386
43:30.200 --> 43:32.657
For the survival of the Yu Army,

387
43:32.657 --> 43:35.706
and to keep the people of Nanhuai from being slaughtered,

388
43:35.706 --> 43:37.126
I'm ordering...

389
43:38.586 --> 43:40.387
An immediate pullback of our defenses.

390
43:40.387 --> 43:42.206
Hold only, no attacks.

391
43:42.206 --> 43:44.646
At the same time, draw up a withdrawal plan.

392
43:44.646 --> 43:49.646
If the situation becomes unmanageable, we move south of the Yangtze at once,

393
43:49.646 --> 43:52.867
preserve our strength, and plan for later.

394
43:52.867 --> 43:54.166
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

395
44:08.086 --> 44:10.520
Is there anything else you want to say?

396
44:10.520 --> 44:12.520
We can't just defend.

397
44:13.726 --> 44:15.407
Why not?

398
44:18.840 --> 44:22.706
The Nanjing Government is dragging its feet on resisting Japan because it wants the Japanese

399
44:22.706 --> 44:26.507
to weaken the regional warlords and the Communists.

400
44:27.120 --> 44:28.840
But we're soldiers.

401
44:28.840 --> 44:32.373
If Wubeikou falls, North China is lost.

402
44:32.373 --> 44:34.606
Now, to hold back

403
44:34.606 --> 44:39.080
is to push the people behind us straight into the Japanese guns.

404
44:39.080 --> 44:42.197
Do you think I don't know what Nanjing is up to?

405
44:42.197 --> 44:48.266
I know, so I want to keep the Yu Army alive.

406
44:48.266 --> 44:52.046
In times like these, guns are our leverage.

407
44:52.046 --> 44:53.566
If we go reinforce them,

408
44:53.566 --> 44:58.427
we'll burn through everything we have,

409
44:58.427 --> 45:00.680
and I'll be a commander with no army.

410
45:00.680 --> 45:04.740
A commander without soldiers is nothing.

411
45:05.566 --> 45:12.086
I wouldn't even be able to protect the Yu family, let alone protecting the people.

412
45:12.086 --> 45:14.440
If the nation falls,

413
45:14.440 --> 45:16.840
what good are tens of thousands of guns in your hands?

414
45:16.840 --> 45:18.927
Even if you keep your troops,

415
45:18.927 --> 45:21.746
they'll be puppet soldiers working for the Japanese.

416
45:22.760 --> 45:28.110
Do you really want to be a puppet,

417
45:28.110 --> 45:31.200
governing the soldiers and people who trust us under Japanese control?

418
45:31.200 --> 45:34.810
When that day comes, we'll all be slaves of a conquered nation.

419
45:34.810 --> 45:36.600
You're out of line.

420
45:50.840 --> 45:55.226
Going head-to-head with them is a dead end.

421
46:06.226 --> 46:08.867
If the road ahead leads to a dead end,

422
46:09.880 --> 46:13.040
then I'd rather die charging the enemy

423
46:13.880 --> 46:16.600
than die running away.

424
46:16.600 --> 46:18.307
What are you planning to do?

425
46:18.307 --> 46:23.027
Since you insist on defending and won't commit your troops to reinforce them,

426
46:24.160 --> 46:27.760
then I'll take the 9th Corps and the 7th Corps, the ones I built with my own hands,

427
46:27.760 --> 46:31.427
north right now and reinforce Wubeikou.

428
46:31.427 --> 46:36.586
Chang Xuan, you're going there to die.

429
46:38.686 --> 46:40.126
Commander-in-Chief.

430
46:42.106 --> 46:43.427
Take care of yourself.
